<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00CL">Exercise <span data-tag="00CL">2.1.2.20</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a monoidal category with unit object $\mathbf{1}$. Show that, for every pair of objects $X,Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the diagrams </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X \otimes (Y \otimes \mathbf{1}) \ar [rr]^{\alpha _{X,Y,\mathbf{1}} } \ar [dr]_{\operatorname{id}_ X \otimes \rho _{Y}} &amp;  &amp;  (X \otimes Y) \otimes \mathbf{1} \ar [dl]^{ \rho _{ X \otimes Y} } \\ &amp;  X \otimes Y &amp;  } \]
</div>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \mathbf{1} \otimes (X \otimes Y) \ar [dr]_{\lambda _{X \otimes Y}} \ar [rr]^{ \alpha _{ \mathbf{1}, X, Y} } &amp;  &amp;  ( \mathbf{1} \otimes X) \otimes Y \ar [dl]^{ \lambda _ X \otimes \operatorname{id}_ Y} \\ &amp;  X \otimes Y &amp;  } \]
</div>
<p> are commutative (for a more general statement, see Proposition <a data-tag="0080" href="/tag/0080">2.2.1.15</a>). </p>
</article>
